# G9POS — Coding Standards

## Flutter — Structure
```
apps/mobile/lib/
  core/
    database/       ← Drift schema, DAOs
    sync/           ← sync queue, flusher, event definitions
    auth/           ← JWT cache, offline auth, PIN
    hardware/       ← scanner/printer HAL
    theme/          ← AppColors, AppTextStyles, AppSpacing
    utils/          ← CurrencyFormatter, ShopDateUtils, UuidGenerator
  features/
    auth/ pos/ products/ inventory/ sales/
    expenses/ suppliers/ reports/ settings/
  shared/
    widgets/        ← reusable UI components
    providers/      ← app-wide Riverpod providers
    router/         ← GoRouter config
```

Each feature folder: `providers/`, `repositories/`, `screens/`, `widgets/`

## Flutter — The Repository Pattern
UI → Provider → Repository → Drift DAO. Never skip layers.

```dart
// Repository: local SQLite first, then sync queue
class ProductRepository {
  Future<void> saveProduct(ProductsCompanion product) async {
    await _db.productDao.upsert(product);           // 1. local first
    await _syncQueue.enqueue(                        // 2. then queue
      eventType: product.id.present ? 'PRODUCT_UPDATED' : 'PRODUCT_CREATED',
      payload: product.toJson(),
      referenceId: product.id.value,
    );
  }
  Stream<List<Product>> watchAll() =>               // reads from local SQLite
    _db.productDao.watchAllActive();
}

// Provider
final productRepositoryProvider = Provider<ProductRepository>((ref) =>
  ProductRepository(ref.watch(appDatabaseProvider), ref.watch(syncQueueDaoProvider)));

// Screen — never imports Drift or DAO directly
class ProductListScreen extends ConsumerWidget {
  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {
    return ref.watch(productListProvider).when(
      data: (list) => ProductGrid(products: list),
      loading: () => const ProductGridSkeleton(),
      error: (e, _) => const ErrorMessage(message: 'Could not load products'),
    );
  }
}
```

## Flutter — Naming
```dart
// Files: snake_case
product_repository.dart

// Classes: PascalCase
class ProductRepository {}

// Variables/functions: camelCase
final productList = <Product>[];

// Constants: camelCase with k prefix
const kScanThresholdMs = 100;

// Providers: end with Provider
final productListProvider = StreamProvider<List<Product>>(...);
```

## Flutter — Error Handling
```dart
// ✅ Correct — catch, log, plain language state
Future<void> saveProduct(ProductsCompanion product) async {
  try {
    await _repository.saveProduct(product);
  } on DriftException catch (e, stack) {
    _logger.error('save product failed', error: e, stackTrace: stack);
    state = state.copyWith(error: 'Could not save product. Try again.');
  } catch (e, stack) {
    _logger.error('unexpected error', error: e, stackTrace: stack);
    state = state.copyWith(error: 'Something went wrong. Try again.');
  }
}

// ❌ Wrong
await _repository.saveProduct(product); // unhandled — crashes
```

Every async function touching DB, network, or hardware is wrapped in try/catch. Never rethrow from a UI action handler.

## Flutter — Drift Rules
```dart
// Every read filters soft-deleted records
Stream<List<Product>> watchAllActive() =>
  (select(products)..where((p) => p.deletedAt.isNull())).watch();

// Every inventory_events read also filters rejected
Future<int> computeStock(String productId) async =>
  (selectOnly(inventoryEvents)
    ..addColumns([inventoryEvents.quantityDelta.sum()])
    ..where(inventoryEvents.productId.equals(productId))
    ..where(inventoryEvents.rejectedAt.isNull())) // required — G1
  .map((r) => r.read(inventoryEvents.quantityDelta.sum()) ?? 0)
  .getSingle();

// Never use auto-increment — always UUID
TextColumn get id => text()();  // UUID set by app before insert
```

